@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title House rules — proveo's conventions in every session, without touching a repository

' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile,
'         defs/opencode/Dockerfile

node "proveo image" as IMG <<host>> {
  file "/opt/proveo/AGENTS\.md\nthis repo's conventions, baked in" as SRC <<db>>
}

node "Managed policy path (baked, root-owned)" as MANAGED <<host>> {
  file "claudecode → ""/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE\.md""\nhighest tier · cannot be excluded" as POLICY <<app>>
}
node "Agent home (written by the seed)" as HOME <<host>> {
  file "opencode → ""\.config/opencode/AGENTS\.md""" as USERFILE <<app>>
}
folder "Operator's repository" as REPO <<error>>

component "**route** — ""_house_rules_target""\none row per supported harness" as ROUTE <<app>>
component "**write** — ""_proveo_write_block""\nmarked region only" as WRITE <<app>>
component "agent — merges user + project" as AGENT <<app>>

SRC ARROW_MAIN POLICY : baked at BUILD time (uid 0)
SRC ARROW_MAIN ROUTE
ROUTE ARROW_MAIN WRITE : only where a user-level file EXISTS
WRITE ARROW_MAIN USERFILE
POLICY ARROW_MAIN AGENT : loaded FIRST, every session
USERFILE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : loaded every session
REPO ARROW_MAIN AGENT : project rules, ranked HIGHER
ROUTE ARROW_ERROR REPO : never written to

note bottom of REPO
  **The workspace is not ours to seed.** Writing an AGENTS\.md there mutates the
  operator's checkout, competes with one they already wrote, and cannot apply at
  all when theirs exists. The USER layer has none of those problems: both
  harnesses below MERGE it with the project's instead of choosing, and both rank
  the project's higher — so a repo can always overrule the house.
end note

note right of ROUTE
  **Every supported harness gets a row, including the empty ones**, so silence is
  a decision a reader can check rather than an oversight.

  ""claudecode"" NOT here — ""/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE\.md"", baked by the Dockerfile.
              The MANAGED POLICY tier loads before the user and project files and
              cannot be excluded by ""claudeMdExcludes"" at any settings layer,
              which is what "always applies" actually requires. The home file
              this table writes is the LOWEST tier, and a project CLAUDE\.md
              outranks it — so it could not have guaranteed anything.
  ""opencode""   ~/\.config/opencode/AGENTS\.md — the documented global file;
              instructions render global first, then project on top.
  ""cursor""     NONE. cursor-agent reads ""\.cursor/rules"" and a project-root
              AGENTS\.md/CLAUDE\.md; its global "User Rules" live in the IDE
              settings UI, not a file the CLI reads.
  ""cecli""      NONE established. It seeds a PROJECT CONVENTIONS\.md from its own
              defaults; guessing a user-level path writes a file nothing reads.
end note

note bottom of WRITE
  The destination may already hold hand-written content, so the region proveo
  owns is delimited by HTML comment markers and everything outside them is
  copied through untouched. The block is REPLACED on every start rather than
  appended, which is what keeps a long-lived proveo home from growing a new copy
  per run. ""PROVEO_HOUSE_RULES=off"" skips the whole step.
end note

note top of SRC
  Baked into the image rather than mounted: it must be present on BOTH backends,
  and a file the sandbox cannot edit cannot be edited by the agent either.
end note
@enduml
